WEBVTT

00:06.459 --> 00:07.589
Master Masachika.

00:11.589 --> 00:12.071
Master Masachika.

00:14.339 --> 00:15.509
Ayano.

00:15.071 --> 00:17.026
What's the matter?

00:17.339 --> 00:19.379
I'm sorry to bother you suddenly.

00:19.076 --> 00:22.067
May I have a moment of your time?

00:23.379 --> 00:24.379
Sure.

00:24.071 --> 00:26.017
Thank you.

00:26.629 --> 00:27.046
This way, please.

00:28.021 --> 00:29.008
She's still the same,

00:29.879 --> 00:31.067
just like a ninja.

01:53.879 --> 01:55.042
(Alya Sometimes Hides Her Feelings in Russian)

02:03.709 --> 02:05.001
(Episode 7: A Storm Is Coming)
Master Masachika,

02:05.009 --> 02:06.379
(Episode 7: A Storm Is Coming)
thank you for your precious--

02:06.459 --> 02:07.459
No need for this.

02:08.005 --> 02:09.005
What is it?

02:09.129 --> 02:10.669
Forgive my rudeness.

02:11.021 --> 02:12.169
Well then.

02:12.509 --> 02:13.759
Master Masachika,

02:13.084 --> 02:16.669
I heard that you're running
for president with Mistress Kujou.

02:17.005 --> 02:19.379
May I know if this is true?

02:19.629 --> 02:20.071
Yes.

02:23.419 --> 02:24.759
The head of the family

02:25.129 --> 02:28.259
is very upset about this.

02:29.259 --> 02:31.084
Why is Master Masachika,
who abandoned the Suou family,

02:31.919 --> 02:34.629
still getting in Mistress Yuki's way?

02:34.071 --> 02:36.919
The head of the family
was furious when he said that.

02:37.009 --> 02:38.669
That old geezer.

02:39.509 --> 02:43.005
He told me not to think of myself
as a Suou after I left that house

02:43.379 --> 02:46.084
and also not to tell anyone
that I'm Yuki's older brother.

02:46.919 --> 02:49.005
But now he's treating me
like family again?

02:49.629 --> 02:51.629
Don't mess with me, old geezer.

02:52.034 --> 02:53.419
So?

02:53.509 --> 02:56.919
Did he send you
to find out my true intentions?

02:57.003 --> 02:59.096
No, this is my own will.

03:00.509 --> 03:02.021
As Mistress Yuki's retainer,

03:02.003 --> 03:04.419
if someone opposes her,

03:04.509 --> 03:06.919
I must determine
the other party's true intentions.

03:07.009 --> 03:08.034
You sure are loyal.

03:08.419 --> 03:09.055
Are you a samurai?

03:10.509 --> 03:11.629
I have

03:11.071 --> 03:13.021
always believed

03:13.008 --> 03:17.021
that Master Masachika
would never do anything

03:17.003 --> 03:18.919
to make Mistress Yuki sad.

03:19.879 --> 03:22.003
Could it be that I was mistaken?

03:22.669 --> 03:26.008
I didn't join the election
to go against Yuki.

03:27.003 --> 03:28.021
It's just that

03:28.003 --> 03:30.419
I ended up becoming Yuki's opponent.

03:30.096 --> 03:32.379
Regardless of the order,

03:32.046 --> 03:34.096
the fact that you're opposing her
doesn't change.

03:35.379 --> 03:37.009
For Master Masachika,

03:37.169 --> 03:39.003
is running with Mistress Kujou

03:39.071 --> 03:41.379
so important that you can

03:41.046 --> 03:44.046
betray Mistress Yuki and even hurt her?

03:45.046 --> 03:46.046
Yes.

03:48.005 --> 03:51.059
I'll do my best to help Alya
become the student council president.

03:52.169 --> 03:53.059
I made a promise to her.

03:54.129 --> 03:57.379
Does that stem from some special emotions?

03:57.084 --> 03:59.669
Could it be that you have feelings--

03:59.759 --> 04:00.669
No.

04:01.005 --> 04:03.034
I'm doing this because I want to.

04:05.055 --> 04:07.169
So please relay this to Grandpa.

04:07.509 --> 04:09.759
"Don't blame Yuki for this."

04:10.021 --> 04:11.759
"If you have any complaints,"

04:12.009 --> 04:14.034
"say it to me directly."

04:17.129 --> 04:18.959
As you wish.

04:19.509 --> 04:22.005
Please allow me to ask one last thing.

04:22.629 --> 04:23.839
Master Masachika,

04:23.092 --> 04:26.259
have your feelings for Mistress Yuki

04:26.339 --> 04:28.259
remained unchanged?

04:29.005 --> 04:30.129
To me, Yuki

04:30.209 --> 04:33.129
is the most important person in the world.

04:33.509 --> 04:35.005
Even now, that's how I feel.

04:36.092 --> 04:38.129
So, do me a favor.

04:38.008 --> 04:40.042
Please support her well.

04:42.042 --> 04:43.759
As you wish.

04:44.089 --> 04:47.839
I'm glad to hear your thoughts,
Master Masachika.

04:50.989 --> 04:52.409
I shall take my leave now.

04:55.057 --> 04:58.082
Or did I disappoint her?

05:01.659 --> 05:02.529
Ta-da!

05:02.609 --> 05:04.082
Look, it's this week's
gravure magazine cover!

05:05.159 --> 05:07.045
Hey, Masachika. Who's your favorite?

05:07.779 --> 05:10.002
To be honest,
I don't know anything about idols.

05:10.279 --> 05:12.609
Don't talk like an old man.

05:12.007 --> 05:14.279
Just look at their appearance.

05:15.359 --> 05:16.909
Let me see.

05:17.359 --> 05:19.779
Well, if I had to choose one of them,

05:19.859 --> 05:20.859
it'd be her, I guess.

05:22.659 --> 05:24.279
The girl Masachika picked

05:24.359 --> 05:25.909
kind of resembles Senior Kujou.

05:27.032 --> 05:28.489
Is that so?

05:30.029 --> 05:32.007
Now that you mention it,
she does look like her.

05:32.779 --> 05:35.489
Masachika, is Senior Kujou your type?

05:35.057 --> 05:36.859
No, not at all.

05:37.279 --> 05:39.279
Besides, Masha has a boyfriend.

05:39.359 --> 05:41.409
So if she didn't, would you go after her?

05:41.659 --> 05:44.029
By the way,
when did you start using her nickname?

05:44.109 --> 05:45.859
Aren't you getting too close to her?

05:45.095 --> 05:48.057
No, it's just a coincidence.

05:48.095 --> 05:51.659
I've never looked at Masha that way.

05:58.002 --> 05:59.095
Beast.

06:01.032 --> 06:03.659
You're a member of the student council.

06:03.739 --> 06:06.109
Do you think you can bring this to school?

06:06.359 --> 06:07.529
Well, that's...

06:08.109 --> 06:11.032
Strictly speaking, Takeshi brought it here.

06:11.409 --> 06:13.029
Still, be careful.

06:13.409 --> 06:14.045
Okay.

06:20.359 --> 06:21.095
Let me change the question.

06:22.029 --> 06:24.239
Have you ever thought about dating Suou?

06:25.002 --> 06:27.609
No, I can never date her.

06:27.007 --> 06:28.529
Why?

06:28.609 --> 06:30.029
You're asking me why...

06:30.989 --> 06:32.029
In any case,

06:32.109 --> 06:33.239
if I'm going to date,

06:33.032 --> 06:35.609
I'd like someone I can be friends with.

06:35.909 --> 06:37.409
In other words,

06:37.489 --> 06:39.109
someone like me?

06:40.002 --> 06:41.032
Masachika?

06:41.409 --> 06:42.239
What's wrong?

06:42.032 --> 06:43.032
It's nothing.

06:46.409 --> 06:47.057
Right.

06:47.659 --> 06:50.989
Also, girls with cute smiles
are charming too.

06:53.359 --> 06:55.409
People who don't smile with their eyes

06:55.489 --> 06:57.359
do seem unapproachable.

06:59.002 --> 07:01.095
Indeed, their everyday attitude
is really important.

07:04.489 --> 07:05.989
You should be more considerate.

07:06.007 --> 07:07.529
Alya will get hurt.

07:07.609 --> 07:08.045
- What?
- What?

07:08.529 --> 07:09.609
It's okay.

07:09.082 --> 07:11.779
I have friends anyway.

07:11.859 --> 07:13.032
I don't mind being unlikeable.

07:13.409 --> 07:15.007
Anyway, make up for it. Hurry up.

07:15.779 --> 07:16.859
Okay.

07:17.779 --> 07:18.989
However!

07:19.007 --> 07:22.007
A beautiful girl like Princess Alya
wouldn't mind something like this, right?

07:22.779 --> 07:24.007
- That's adding fuel to the fire!
- That's adding fuel to the fire!

07:24.159 --> 07:25.029
What?

07:26.529 --> 07:27.659
So is this

07:27.739 --> 07:29.359
how you have always viewed me?

07:29.739 --> 07:31.029
I'm truly sorry.

07:31.109 --> 07:35.007
I'm just a cold and unlovable girl,
who only has her looks to offer.

07:35.159 --> 07:37.045
No, you're not that bad.

07:38.032 --> 07:39.529
I'd better confiscate

07:39.609 --> 07:40.659
this magazine.

07:46.279 --> 07:47.045
Come in.

07:47.007 --> 07:49.029
Excuse me.

07:52.007 --> 07:53.859
So, are you satisfied now?

07:54.239 --> 07:55.159
Yes.

07:55.239 --> 07:56.082
Sure enough, Master Masachika

07:56.909 --> 07:59.529
is still the esteemed
Master Masachika I admire.

07:59.609 --> 08:01.159
I'm glad to hear that.

08:01.239 --> 08:02.659
What did my brother say?

08:02.909 --> 08:04.529
Master Masachika said

08:04.609 --> 08:08.029
that he hadn't changed his mind
about running with Mistress Kujou.

08:08.109 --> 08:09.002
I thought so.

08:09.909 --> 08:10.082
Also,

08:10.909 --> 08:14.002
he asked me to relay this
to the head of the family.

08:14.489 --> 08:17.109
"If you have any complaints,
say it to me directly."

08:17.002 --> 08:19.032
Well, that's...

08:19.007 --> 08:20.859
How bold of him.

08:20.095 --> 08:23.109
It seems you're serious too, brother.

08:23.045 --> 08:24.409
Yes.

08:24.489 --> 08:25.989
Such a wonderful spirit

08:26.007 --> 08:27.989
makes my uterus tremble.

08:29.739 --> 08:32.109
Really? Even your uterus is trembling?

08:32.002 --> 08:33.029
Yes.

08:33.409 --> 08:34.319
Excuse me.

08:34.409 --> 08:36.029
Just to be clear,

08:36.011 --> 08:40.069
Ayano, you're not in love
with my brother, are you?

08:40.409 --> 08:41.099
Yes.

08:42.069 --> 08:43.909
Just as I respect
and admire Mistress Yuki,

08:43.099 --> 08:46.659
I feel the same about Master Masachika.

08:46.074 --> 08:49.199
I have no romantic feelings for him.

08:49.279 --> 08:50.049
Is that so?

08:50.949 --> 08:52.659
I don't have

08:52.074 --> 08:55.086
the arrogant thought of
"I want to be your girlfriend."

08:56.024 --> 08:58.279
As long as I can be used as a tool,

08:58.036 --> 08:59.569
I'm satisfied.

08:59.086 --> 09:02.199
You're just an ordinary Super M,
aren't you?

09:02.279 --> 09:03.074
I'm very sorry.

09:03.819 --> 09:06.029
What does "Super M" mean?

09:06.011 --> 09:06.099
What?

09:07.069 --> 09:09.036
It means Super Maid.

09:09.449 --> 09:11.569
The abbreviation is Super M.

09:11.909 --> 09:13.279
Thank you for the compliment.

09:14.529 --> 09:15.659
It's my honor.

09:15.074 --> 09:19.036
I'll continue to work hard
to become a great Super M.

09:20.819 --> 09:22.949
You just said something amazing.

09:23.659 --> 09:24.529
Right.

09:24.061 --> 09:25.949
There's one last thing.

09:26.029 --> 09:27.159
What is it?

09:27.659 --> 09:29.074
Master Masachika said

09:30.319 --> 09:31.036
that Mistress Yuki

09:31.449 --> 09:34.819
is still the most important person
in the world to him.

09:42.029 --> 09:43.029
Mistress Yuki?

09:49.044 --> 09:50.519
That was close!

09:50.609 --> 09:54.729
I almost shout out my love for my brother
in the center of the school premises!

09:56.109 --> 09:57.109
Good grief.

09:57.019 --> 09:59.899
I can't stand my cute brother.

10:02.069 --> 10:03.081
Come to think of it,

10:04.979 --> 10:07.609
he's actually serious
about competing with me.

10:08.359 --> 10:09.069
Not bad.

10:09.769 --> 10:11.479
Things are getting interesting.

10:12.269 --> 10:15.109
To be honest,
Alya alone is no match for me.

10:15.044 --> 10:17.019
Most of the freshmen

10:17.269 --> 10:19.979
seem to think
that Mistress Yuki will be elected.

10:20.069 --> 10:22.269
As for Mistress Kujou,

10:22.769 --> 10:24.609
to be honest,

10:24.069 --> 10:28.019
"A transfer student who doesn't know
President Suou from junior high school

10:28.269 --> 10:30.006
is doing something reckless."

10:30.359 --> 10:32.006
That's everyone's impression of her.

10:33.044 --> 10:35.019
How merciless.

10:35.056 --> 10:36.479
Well then,

10:36.056 --> 10:40.479
how will my brother turn the tables?

10:41.269 --> 10:42.649
You look very happy.

10:42.729 --> 10:43.979
Indeed, I am.

10:44.359 --> 10:46.359
After all, this is my chance
to have a showdown

10:46.044 --> 10:49.609
with my genius brother
who's also a Suou family prodigy.

10:50.229 --> 10:54.006
I could never beat my brother
no matter what I did.

10:54.149 --> 10:58.859
But now, he's going to challenge me
with this strong partner, Alya.

10:59.229 --> 11:00.094
I'm so excited.

11:01.019 --> 11:02.094
These are worthy opponents.

11:03.019 --> 11:06.149
All right, I'll do my best to defeat them.

11:11.309 --> 11:12.064
By the way, Ayano.

11:12.719 --> 11:14.429
What is it, Mistress Yuki?

11:17.309 --> 11:18.719
Don't you think I look like

11:18.809 --> 11:20.809
the final boss right now?

11:24.059 --> 11:25.719
(Student Council Office)

11:29.679 --> 11:30.719
Raise.

11:33.179 --> 11:35.099
Fold. I won't call.

11:35.179 --> 11:36.809
Really?

11:37.026 --> 11:39.219
Actually, I have a high card.

11:39.309 --> 11:41.309
I was right to bluff just now.

11:41.039 --> 11:42.349
What?

11:42.076 --> 11:44.039
Oh my, Alya.

11:44.469 --> 11:46.219
It's so close.

11:53.679 --> 11:56.929
Sure enough,
Suou's skills are far superior.

11:57.001 --> 12:00.179
That kind of psychological warfare
is Yuki's forte, after all.

12:01.469 --> 12:02.076
That's part of it,

12:02.849 --> 12:05.809
but it's mainly because Alya
is too easy to read, right?

12:05.089 --> 12:07.099
Sarashina.

12:07.179 --> 12:09.679
You voiced my hidden thoughts
that I dare not express.

12:09.076 --> 12:10.599
What?

12:10.679 --> 12:11.076
I'm kind of sorry.

12:13.849 --> 12:16.064
Alya unexpectedly wears
her heart on her sleeve.

12:17.349 --> 12:21.059
I thought she was
less emotional than her sister.

12:21.429 --> 12:22.429
Maybe

12:22.051 --> 12:25.469
Masha is the one who's harder to read.

12:26.849 --> 12:27.849
That's true.

12:28.309 --> 12:29.064
To be honest,

12:29.719 --> 12:31.969
I can't figure her out either.

12:32.219 --> 12:35.429
She's basically a good kid like Madonna.

12:35.849 --> 12:39.349
But sometimes, her words
and actions are strange.

12:39.429 --> 12:41.064
Masha does have a unique sensibility.

12:42.059 --> 12:43.469
To be precise, a loose screw?

12:43.559 --> 12:45.349
You voiced my hidden thoughts again!

12:45.599 --> 12:46.849
I'm sorry.

12:47.099 --> 12:48.026
Mistress Sarashina.

12:49.429 --> 12:51.429
Would you like something to drink?

12:53.099 --> 12:55.064
You're good at hiding your presence.

12:56.599 --> 12:57.969
I'm fine.

12:58.059 --> 12:59.014
There's still some left.

12:59.219 --> 13:00.051
I see.

13:00.929 --> 13:03.059
By the way, is this behavior and conduct

13:03.014 --> 13:05.076
something you must learn
as Suou's retainer?

13:05.849 --> 13:06.679
Yes.

13:06.076 --> 13:08.051
I learned it from my grandparents.

13:09.719 --> 13:10.929
Ayano's grandparents

13:11.001 --> 13:12.809
used to work for Yuki's family.

13:13.089 --> 13:15.219
So, your parents too?

13:15.559 --> 13:18.219
No, my parents are office workers.

13:18.076 --> 13:20.001
I see.

13:20.026 --> 13:23.719
I became a retainer
because I admired my grandparents,

13:23.809 --> 13:26.309
not because it's a family business.

13:27.969 --> 13:30.469
By the way, when did you
start being a retainer?

13:30.559 --> 13:34.469
I don't know exactly when I started,

13:34.559 --> 13:36.679
but I decided to become a retainer

13:36.076 --> 13:39.179
when I was in second grade.

13:39.469 --> 13:40.599
That's too early.

13:40.679 --> 13:43.179
That's how much I admired my grandparents.

13:43.599 --> 13:44.429
And

13:44.051 --> 13:45.039
Masa...

13:46.349 --> 13:50.679
It just so happened
that Mistress Yuki was the perfect master.

13:52.026 --> 13:53.969
Ayano, come here.

13:54.064 --> 13:55.599
I'm sorry.

13:55.679 --> 13:58.039
I misspoke just now, Master Masachika.

13:58.469 --> 14:01.429
It's fine. You just need to be careful.

14:01.076 --> 14:02.089
It's just...

14:03.089 --> 14:05.559
(Respect and Admiration)

14:05.679 --> 14:07.969
She has such determined eyes!

14:08.059 --> 14:09.059
Why?

14:09.014 --> 14:10.076
Is she not angry anymore?

14:10.849 --> 14:13.179
Where did she improve her likeability?

14:13.064 --> 14:15.559
Is doing things quietly

14:15.064 --> 14:17.429
another skill as a retainer?

14:17.051 --> 14:18.349
Yes.

14:18.429 --> 14:21.014
My grandparents always tell me

14:21.219 --> 14:22.051
that as a servant,

14:22.599 --> 14:25.026
I have to work hard to become air.

14:37.679 --> 14:38.809
Ayano.

14:38.089 --> 14:41.001
Can you pour me some juice too?

14:41.309 --> 14:43.064
Forgive my negligence, Mistress Mariya.

14:44.809 --> 14:47.719
Alya just scolded me for being annoying.

14:51.059 --> 14:53.001
Hey, is this going to be okay?

14:53.099 --> 14:54.599
They won't fight, right?

14:54.679 --> 14:56.099
I think they'll be fine.

14:56.809 --> 14:59.051
Alya seems to be enjoying it.

14:59.089 --> 15:02.014
It looks like she's having fun.
That's rare.

15:02.219 --> 15:03.039
You're right.

15:03.469 --> 15:05.099
Oh, you can tell?

15:05.179 --> 15:06.469
I can tell.

15:08.099 --> 15:09.309
Having fun?

15:09.076 --> 15:10.809
That expression?

15:13.099 --> 15:14.089
Oh my, is it finished?

15:15.026 --> 15:17.219
I'll go buy some more.

15:17.309 --> 15:19.001
Then, I...

15:19.099 --> 15:20.469
It's okay.

15:20.559 --> 15:23.099
Ayano, you're the heroine today.

15:24.059 --> 15:25.071
After all, you and I

15:25.799 --> 15:27.096
are the protagonists
of this welcome party.

15:28.259 --> 15:30.669
As a girl, you're naturally the heroine.

15:30.759 --> 15:32.259
That's right.

15:32.759 --> 15:33.879
Well, hero,

15:33.096 --> 15:35.799
please escort me.

15:35.879 --> 15:36.084
Why?

15:36.096 --> 15:38.629
(Welcome Party
for New Student Council Members)

15:40.049 --> 15:42.259
I'm going to buy some drinks.
What do you want?

15:42.549 --> 15:44.759
I want cafe au lait.

15:45.419 --> 15:47.046
Not the white one, the brown one.

15:47.084 --> 15:49.259
I want red bean soup.

15:49.046 --> 15:50.096
I want soda.

15:51.049 --> 15:51.879
I want cola...

15:51.096 --> 15:53.509
No, ginger ale.

15:53.096 --> 15:55.759
I'll just have water.

15:56.049 --> 15:58.549
Well then, I want lemon tea.

15:58.096 --> 16:01.009
Masha, you don't have to tell me, right?

16:01.169 --> 16:02.379
We're going together.

16:02.046 --> 16:04.049
Right.

16:04.759 --> 16:05.759
Well,

16:05.084 --> 16:08.046
so soda, ginger ale, lemon tea,

16:08.549 --> 16:09.879
and brown cafe au lait,

16:09.096 --> 16:12.049
as well as red bean soup
and water. Got it.

16:12.071 --> 16:13.084
- What?
- What?

16:19.021 --> 16:20.259
Kuze,

16:20.059 --> 16:22.419
thank you once again.

16:22.509 --> 16:24.049
Why did you suddenly say that?

16:24.509 --> 16:28.059
Thank you for running
for student council president with Alya.

16:29.021 --> 16:32.759
I'm sure Alya is overjoyed about it.

16:33.009 --> 16:34.009
It's nothing much.

16:34.169 --> 16:36.879
And there's no need for you to thank me.

16:37.299 --> 16:38.299
My goodness.

16:38.379 --> 16:40.299
Of course, I should thank you.

16:40.799 --> 16:43.419
Alya had no one to lean on all this time.

16:43.084 --> 16:46.419
There's finally someone
willing to support her.

16:50.379 --> 16:51.059
Are you...

16:52.669 --> 16:53.071
It's nothing.

16:54.169 --> 16:55.879
I was just thinking, Masha.

16:55.096 --> 17:00.379
Are you purposely hiding
your serious side from Alya?

17:05.099 --> 17:06.559
Well, I

17:06.559 --> 17:08.599
don't want to compete with Alya.

17:10.849 --> 17:13.076
Because Alya is a very serious child.

17:13.849 --> 17:15.068
She tries her best in everything she does.

17:16.068 --> 17:20.559
I really like Alya the way she is.

17:39.041 --> 17:41.249
What are you doing?

17:42.041 --> 17:43.249
Is that why

17:43.033 --> 17:45.539
you're playing the role
of a meek older sister?

17:45.062 --> 17:47.499
I'm not pretending.

17:47.999 --> 17:51.039
It's tiring to live in fear
all the time, right?

17:51.709 --> 17:53.749
We need to relax.

17:54.499 --> 17:55.033
But

17:55.041 --> 18:00.033
I don't deny that I tend
to be meek in front of Alya.

18:03.039 --> 18:04.459
(Please don't turn it sideways.
Take it out horizontally.)

18:05.209 --> 18:06.033
Because...

18:06.789 --> 18:08.033
I don't want Alya to be alone.

18:10.058 --> 18:12.209
It's not just sisters.

18:12.499 --> 18:14.999
Siblings have
a very complicated relationship.

18:15.709 --> 18:18.499
They're closer than anyone else,

18:18.058 --> 18:19.709
but because of that,

18:19.789 --> 18:22.012
they can't help but care about each other.

18:22.959 --> 18:23.999
Yes.

18:24.008 --> 18:25.083
I feel the same way.

18:26.066 --> 18:29.959
The reason I don't feel inferior to Yuki

18:30.037 --> 18:31.041
is all thanks to her

18:31.499 --> 18:35.041
always brazenly saying
that she loves her brother the most.

18:35.066 --> 18:37.008
(Brown cafe au lait)

18:37.037 --> 18:40.459
Yuki's eccentric personality
with a strong otaku vibe.

18:40.539 --> 18:43.041
Is she also playing the role
of a silly little sister?

18:44.037 --> 18:46.999
No, I'm sure that's her true self.

18:47.083 --> 18:49.209
Masha,

18:49.289 --> 18:50.789
you're such a good sister.

18:51.959 --> 18:53.008
Yes.

18:53.016 --> 18:54.058
I may not look like it,

18:54.066 --> 18:56.087
but I'm a good sister.

18:57.709 --> 18:58.999
Keep what we discussed

18:59.008 --> 19:00.058
a secret from Alya.

19:01.039 --> 19:02.037
I won't tell her.

19:02.459 --> 19:04.016
Even if I did, she wouldn't believe me.

19:04.539 --> 19:07.749
Who would've thought her own sister
is so serious and mature?

19:07.083 --> 19:08.789
Oh dear.

19:09.039 --> 19:13.039
Aren't you hiding
your serious side as well?

19:15.033 --> 19:16.066
The reason I'm doing this

19:16.749 --> 19:18.749
isn't as impressive as yours.

19:19.012 --> 19:21.459
I'm just taking good care of myself.

19:22.062 --> 19:24.749
I just want to live an easy life

19:24.083 --> 19:26.459
so I'm playing a frivolous character

19:26.539 --> 19:28.083
to avoid anyone from relying on me.

19:29.033 --> 19:30.062
Please don't mind me.

19:36.709 --> 19:38.039
There, there.

19:38.062 --> 19:40.033
You're doing your best.

19:40.749 --> 19:41.749
It's okay.

19:42.012 --> 19:43.091
I'm sure you'll be fine, Kuze.

19:44.083 --> 19:46.083
I didn't...

19:46.091 --> 19:48.091
You're a boy, after all.

19:48.999 --> 19:50.012
You're amazing.

19:52.709 --> 19:54.209
I wonder why.

19:54.709 --> 19:57.039
When I face Masha,

19:57.012 --> 19:59.062
I can't help but let my guard down.

20:03.087 --> 20:05.499
Alisa Kujou.

20:10.459 --> 20:11.091
Sorry for the sudden visit.

20:12.037 --> 20:14.058
I'm Sayaka Taniyama from Class F.

20:15.289 --> 20:17.087
Do you have a minute?

20:20.016 --> 20:21.066
Sayaka Taniyama.

20:22.016 --> 20:23.066
I remember that in junior high,

20:23.749 --> 20:26.041
she competed with Yuki for the presidency.

20:26.499 --> 20:27.058
Kujou.

20:28.039 --> 20:32.789
Are you really going to join
the presidential election with Kuze?

20:33.016 --> 20:34.789
Yes. What's the matter?

20:36.749 --> 20:39.749
To actually do something so vulgar,

20:39.083 --> 20:41.062
aren't you ashamed?

20:41.709 --> 20:42.058
What?

20:42.083 --> 20:47.249
You stole the person
who Suou wanted to invite as her partner.

20:47.033 --> 20:48.066
Are you causing trouble?

20:48.749 --> 20:50.012
What?

20:50.209 --> 20:52.008
What do you mean?

20:52.016 --> 20:53.087
Are you saying I used dirty tricks

20:53.959 --> 20:56.058
to get Kuze on my side?

20:56.066 --> 20:57.066
Didn't you?

20:58.041 --> 21:00.091
I don't know how you did it,

21:00.999 --> 21:04.008
but you chose that pathetic Kuze
as your partner

21:04.016 --> 21:07.039
to make Suou angry, didn't you?

21:07.012 --> 21:08.249
I didn't!

21:08.033 --> 21:10.012
Alya? Taniyama?

21:13.209 --> 21:14.033
What's happening here?

21:14.041 --> 21:15.959
I don't know either.

21:16.039 --> 21:17.749
She suddenly came to pick a fight,

21:17.083 --> 21:21.039
saying I played dirty
to steal you from Suou.

21:21.289 --> 21:22.058
What's going on?

21:23.008 --> 21:24.499
Well, Taniyama.

21:24.789 --> 21:27.209
I don't know who told you,

21:27.289 --> 21:30.539
but I decided to partner
with Alya on my own.

21:30.091 --> 21:32.749
I can't believe it.

21:33.289 --> 21:35.041
As someone who's utterly pathetic,

21:35.499 --> 21:39.012
why would you team up
with that transfer student?

21:39.041 --> 21:41.033
Wait, you're calling me pathetic.

21:41.058 --> 21:43.062
Well, I won't deny it.

21:44.249 --> 21:45.209
Anyway,

21:45.289 --> 21:47.209
Yuki acknowledges this too.

21:47.289 --> 21:48.959
It's all your misunderstanding.

21:49.459 --> 21:51.041
Since your words have offended Alya,

21:51.499 --> 21:52.789
could you please apologize?

21:55.289 --> 21:56.016
I see.

21:56.459 --> 21:58.289
So you're the one

21:58.037 --> 22:00.016
who should be punished, right?

22:05.091 --> 22:06.999
Kuze.

22:07.008 --> 22:09.789
I'm calling a general meeting
to challenge you.

22:09.087 --> 22:10.789
What?

22:10.087 --> 22:13.209
Did you hear that?
She's calling a general meeting.

22:13.289 --> 22:14.012
Seriously?

22:14.789 --> 22:15.789
What's going on?

22:15.087 --> 22:16.959
A presidential candidate

22:17.039 --> 22:18.037
is calling a general meeting.

22:18.749 --> 22:20.289
No, wait a minute.

22:20.037 --> 22:21.999
Are you serious?

22:22.008 --> 22:24.041
Do you think I'd joke about this?

22:24.499 --> 22:26.037
I'm going to kick you out

22:26.459 --> 22:27.959
of the presidential election.

22:28.289 --> 22:29.012
No.

22:29.209 --> 22:31.539
I'll kick you out of the student council.

22:31.959 --> 22:33.039
Hold on.

22:33.012 --> 22:34.459
Election candidates holding

22:34.539 --> 22:37.016
a general meeting
will affect their standing, right?

22:37.249 --> 22:38.058
Can you not ignore me

22:38.066 --> 22:40.539
and decide on your own?

22:41.039 --> 22:44.249
The eye-candy presidential candidate
who only has good grades

22:44.033 --> 22:45.459
should stay out.

22:45.539 --> 22:46.459
What?

22:46.083 --> 22:49.249
We're a pair in the presidential election.

22:49.033 --> 22:51.459
As a fellow presidential candidate,

22:51.539 --> 22:53.066
if you want to defeat Kuze,

22:54.033 --> 22:56.012
let me take you on.

22:57.039 --> 22:59.091
And here I thought I was sparing you.

23:00.499 --> 23:01.062
Fine.

23:01.709 --> 23:03.066
I'll crush both of you together.

23:04.058 --> 23:06.789
People like you

23:06.087 --> 23:09.012
aren't cut out
for the presidential election.
